  "method": "Each session is generated by the motor-unit simulator and decoded. Every misclassified window is routed: P from overlap of the two classes' tightest training repetitions; B from channel deviation against the intended class's training spread; M from whether an RBF-SVM reference is right where the deployed model is wrong; D from a one-sided CUSUM of distance to the cued class centroid and the running median-frequency shift. A session routes correctly when the plurality of its errors reaches the injected cause. Behavioural routes receive anatomical coaching from an LDA surrogate.",
  "caveat": "Simulated subjects and injected faults. Sessions are cued, so the intended gesture is known. Within-attempt windows are correlated, which inflates CUSUM even in clean sessions. This checks the integrated pipeline on simulator signals; it is not attribution accuracy on recorded or human errors, and the coaching is not validated with people.",
